      After sorting frames increasingly, choose a subsequence of paintings.
      If chosen in increasing order of value, and assigned to increasing frame sizes,
      then adjacent conditions are satisfied.

      We need longest subsequence of paintings such that:
      - sizes can be matched injectively to frames: for k-th chosen painting in order,
        its size <= c[k_assigned]
      - values are nondecreasing.

      Standard DP:
      dp[j] = minimum possible ending value of a valid sequence of length j
              using first processed paintings and first some frames greedily matched.
      But frame capacities differ by position, so a painting can serve as the t-th
      selected painting iff its size <= c[t].

      Process paintings sorted by size ascending. For each painting (s,v), it may be
      placed only at positions t where c[t] >= s. Since c is sorted, let pos be first
      such index. Then it can be used as the t-th selected painting for any t >= pos+1.

      We do LIS-style DP on values:
      best[t] = minimal possible ending value for a valid sequence of length t.
      Initially best[0] = -INF, others = INF.
      For a painting eligible for positions >= L, update from high to low:
         if best[t-1] <= v and t >= L then best[t] = min(best[t], v)

      Complexity O(NM), acceptable only for small constraints, but constraints are
      not provided. We optimize by observing transitions only depend on best[t-1] <= v
      and t >= L. We still use O(NM) as a safe straightforward solution.
    */

    const int INF = 0x3f3f3f3f;
    int *best = (int *)malloc(sizeof(int) * (M + 1));
    for (int i = 0; i <= M; i++) best[i] = INF;
    best[0] = -INF;

    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        int s = p[i].s, v = p[i].v;

        int l = (int)(lower_bound:
            0); /* placeholder to satisfy C syntax avoidance */
        /* manual lower_bound on c for first index with c[idx] >= s */
        int lo = 0, hi = M;
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;
            if (c[mid] >= s) hi = mid;
            else lo = mid + 1;
        }
        l = lo + 1; /* positions are 1-based in DP */

        if (l > M) continue;

        for (int t = M; t >= l; t--) {
            if (best[t - 1] <= v && v < best[t]) {
                best[t] = v;
            }
        }
    }

    int ans = 0;
    for (int t = M; t >= 0; t--) {
        if (best[t] < INF) {
            ans = t;
            break;
        }
    }

    printf("%d\n", ans);

    free(p);
    free(c);
    free(best);
    return 0;
}
